# apps/web (React 19, @types/react@19.2.17) and apps/mobile (React Native's
# bundled React 18, @types/react@18.3.31) intentionally use different React
# major versions in this workspace. By default pnpm hoists every dependency
# into a shared node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules folder so third-party
# packages (e.g. next's internal .d.ts files) can resolve them via
# ancestor-directory lookup without declaring an explicit dependency. With
# two conflicting @types/react versions in the workspace, that shared slot
# is won non-deterministically by whichever version pnpm links last, and
# TypeScript can merge both versions' global JSX/React namespace
# declarations into the same compilation, producing spurious "ReactNode is
# not assignable to ReactPortal" errors (see docs/mobile/readiness-audit.md,
# addendum 2026-07-28). Excluding @types/react and @types/react-dom from
# hoisting removes the ambiguous shared slot entirely: each workspace
# package resolves them strictly through its own scoped dependency
# (apps/web -> 19.2.17, apps/mobile -> 18.3.31), and any third-party file
# that only found them via the shared slot simply stops resolving them
# (harmless -- those files aren't part of our own type graph).
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
